<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">London Missionary Society</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Missionary Society was a Protestant missionary society founded in London in 1795. Its missionaries reached Tahiti and the Society Islands in 1797, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-moffat">Robert Moffat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-livingstone">David Livingstone</a> worked among the Tswana, and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>. They introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and literacy and often advised local rulers, influencing politics in the kingdoms they served.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society.jpg" alt="London Missionary Society" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See filename/description · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bechuana_Congregation_(relates_to_David_Livingstone)_by_The_London_Missionary_Society.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
